From: WordPress Playground contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Use WASI randomness for PHP's CSPRNG

PHP's generic Unix entropy path only attempts getrandom() on a small set of
explicitly recognized kernels and otherwise opens /dev/urandom. Capability-
based WASI guests do not have a /dev/urandom device node.

Use wasi-libc's arc4random_buf() implementation, which obtains secure bytes
from wasi:random/random and supports arbitrary request sizes.
---
 ext/random/random.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ext/random/random.c b/ext/random/random.c
--- a/ext/random/random.c
+++ b/ext/random/random.c
@@ -485,7 +485,9 @@ PHPAPI zend_long php_rand(void)
 /* {{{ php_random_bytes */
 PHPAPI int php_random_bytes(void *bytes, size_t size, bool should_throw)
 {
-#ifdef PHP_WIN32
+#ifdef PHP_WASI
+	arc4random_buf(bytes, size);
+#elif defined(PHP_WIN32)
 	/* Defer to CryptGenRandom on Windows */
 	if (php_win32_get_random_bytes(bytes, size) == FAILURE) {
 		if (should_throw) {
-- 
